From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mepa_apps: guard cli_cmd_* handlers against uport=0 -> PORT_NONE

cli_parm_port_no (mesa/demo/cli.c:206) accepts uport=0 and converts it to
MESA_PORT_NO_NONE (0xFFFFFFFF) via uport2iport() -- the "Port 0 == PORT_NONE"
comment even flags this as intentional, because packet.c and ip.c treat 0
as a "no port" sentinel.

Every cli_cmd_* handler under mepa_apps/ blindly indexes
<inst>->phy_devices[req->port_no] and dereferences the result. For
req->port_no == 0xFFFFFFFF that is a wild pointer, and mesa-demo-void
SIGSEGVs the moment mesa-cmd is invoked with a 0 port argument (e.g.
'mesa-cmd PHY State 0'):

    unhandled signal 11 code 0x1 at 0x00000032ca925760 in mesa-demo-void
    cause: 0x0d (Load page fault)

Add a shared inline helper phy_device_get() that bounds-checks against
inst->phy_device_cnt, plus a PHY_DEVICE_GUARD(inst) convenience macro.
Convert the pre-existing '<inst>->phy_devices[req->port_no] == NULL'
NULL-check idioms in phy25g_diagnostics.c and phy_port_config.c to the
helper, and prepend PHY_DEVICE_GUARD() at the top of every other cli_cmd_*
handler that indexes phy_devices[req->port_no].

Signed-off-by: Vincent Cruz <vicruz@iliad-free.fr>
---
